※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4450

※ The type says how many elements there are and the index is written down, so
※ whether it is one of them is known while compiling.  A program that must fail
※ whenever it is started is one that need not be started.

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    let a: u8⟦4⟧ = ⟦1u8, 2u8, 4u8, 8u8⟧
    a⟦9⟧
